    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44032" root="&#xA;                        نعظ&#xA;                    " body-key="n1">
                        
                            4
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انعظ</span></b> 
                        , (Msb, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنْعَاظٌ</span>, (S, Msb,)
<i>He</i> (a man, Msb, K,) <i>became affected with carnal appetite:</i> (S, Msb, K:) and in like manner
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انعظت</span>, said of a woman. (Msb, K. *) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>His
penis became extended.</i> (M, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رول</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انعظت</span>
                        <i>She</i> (a beast) <i>opened and contracted,
alternately, her vulva;</i> (S, K;) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتعظت</span></b> .
(AO, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  See also 1. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انعظهُ</span>
                        <i>He caused it
to become erect:</i> (S:) or <i>put it in motion:</i> (Msb:)
namely his <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُبّ</span>, (S,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَكَر</span>. (Msb.)

